{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
  "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1956, the money laundering statute, requires an intent to minimize the criminal taint of unlawful proceeds. But the statute does not criminalize concealing money's existence. In this case, Mr. Cuellar's conviction should be reversed for two reasons. First, while the method of the transportation involved may have been designed to conceal, the transportation itself was not. Secondly, while Cuellar may have in fact concealed money itself, he did not conceal the nature, source, location, ownership or control of the unlawful proceeds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Maybe I should ask you this now because you've probably thought about it and I can't work it out. I don't see any problem with the word \"location.\" I thought what you would say is it isn't the transportation in this instance that concealed the location, it's the method of transportation that sealed the location."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Was there a reporting requirement for -- for this shipment. If he had gone to the border, would he -- well, then, a lot of what you're arguing about isn't very important because they could just indict under (ii)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if he -- if he didn't know about the currency-reporting requirement, then he's not guilty under that statute because it requires knowledge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what if there is a wire transfer to a bank in another country because that bank has bank secrecy laws that will make it impossible to ascertain the location of the money once it is there? Does that fall within the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the word \"transportation\" mean the act of transportation across the border or the method of transportation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SCHERTLER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The phrase \"designed in whole or in part\" directs a full examination of the plan, of the way in which the cross-border transportation of these known illegal proceeds was planned out."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SCHERTLER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The purpose of this statute was to prevent criminals from taking their proceeds abroad where they would be outside the reach of all of these controls that have been set up in the United States in order to detect illegal proceeds and use those proceeds to trace back to the crimes and the criminals that generated them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So there is no money laundering if they conceal the proceeds in a suitcase that's in the trunk of the car? Is that enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. SCHERTLER",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SCHERTLER: I think that's enough to get to the jury, and that would be a jury question, Your Honor, yes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask the same basic question of you? Do you think that this line, \"create an appearance of legitimate wealth\" is an essential element of the offense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Beard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That wouldn't give rise to laundering, because all you have there basically is money spending. It's the conduct of the underlying --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Beard, can't you give us something we can get this guy on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can't we get him as an accessory to drug dealing or something? You say he has to walk?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The point -- the point about aiding and abetting something, this money reeks of marijuana, and that was very puzzling to me."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Beard",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice, I know that the -- initially the way this went down was the money that was in his pocket. That's what triggered the -- that's what they said smelled like raw marijuana. And then eventually, they found the drug money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1456",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0ec198957154919837c38cb3f21c7f33c07a634d5ed8fe45c85095a578090285",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ec198957154-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Thank you, Mr. Beard. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:04 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
